---@class mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettings
---@field winner_criteria mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsWinnerCriteria|string The combination that performs the best. This may be determined automatically by click rate, open rate, or total revenue -- or you may choose manually based on the reporting data you find the most valuable. For Multivariate Campaigns testing send_time, winner_criteria is ignored. For Multivariate Campaigns with 'manual' as the winner_criteria, the winner must be chosen in the Mailchimp web application.
---@field wait_time? number The number of minutes to wait before choosing the winning campaign. The value of wait_time must be greater than 0 and in whole hours, specified in minutes.
---@field test_size? number The percentage of recipients to send the test combinations to, must be a value between 10 and 100.
---@field subject_lines? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsSubjectLinesList The possible subject lines to test. If no subject lines are provided, settings.subject_line will be used.
---@field send_times? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsSendTimesList The possible send times to test. The times provided should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. If send_times are provided to test, the test_size will be set to 100% and winner_criteria will be ignored.
---@field from_names? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsFromNamesList The possible from names. The number of from_names provided must match the number of reply_to_addresses. If no from_names are provided, settings.from_name will be used.
---@field reply_to_addresses? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsReplyToAddressesList The possible reply-to addresses. The number of reply_to_addresses provided must match the number of from_names. If no reply_to_addresses are provided, settings.reply_to will be used.

---The possible from names. The number of from_names provided must match the number of reply_to_addresses. If no from_names are provided, settings.from_name will be used.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsFromNamesList string[]

---The possible reply-to addresses. The number of reply_to_addresses provided must match the number of from_names. If no reply_to_addresses are provided, settings.reply_to will be used.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsReplyToAddressesList string[]

---The possible send times to test. The times provided should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. If send_times are provided to test, the test_size will be set to 100% and winner_criteria will be ignored.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsSendTimesList string[]

---The possible subject lines to test. If no subject lines are provided, settings.subject_line will be used.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsSubjectLinesList string[]

---The combination that performs the best. This may be determined automatically by click rate, open rate, or total revenue -- or you may choose manually based on the reporting data you find the most valuable. For Multivariate Campaigns testing send_time, winner_criteria is ignored. For Multivariate Campaigns with 'manual' as the winner_criteria, the winner must be chosen in the Mailchimp web application.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignRequestVariateSettingsWinnerCriteria "opens"|"clicks"|"manual"|"total_revenue"

---@class mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponse
---@field id? string A string that uniquely identifies this campaign.
---@field web_id? number The ID used in the Mailchimp web application. View this campaign in your Mailchimp account at `https://{dc}.admin.mailchimp.com/campaigns/show/?id={web_id}`.
---@field parent_campaign_id? string If this campaign is the child of another campaign, this identifies the parent campaign. For Example, for RSS or Automation children.
---@field type? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseType There are four types of [campaigns](https://mailchimp.com/help/getting-started-with-campaigns/) you can create in Mailchimp. A/B Split campaigns have been deprecated and variate campaigns should be used instead.
---@field create_time? string The date and time the campaign was created in ISO 8601 format.
---@field archive_url? string The link to the campaign's archive version in ISO 8601 format.
---@field long_archive_url? string The original link to the campaign's archive version.
---@field status? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseStatus The current status of the campaign.
---@field emails_sent? number The total number of emails sent for this campaign.
---@field send_time? string The date and time a campaign was sent.
---@field content_type? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseContentType How the campaign's content is put together.
---@field needs_block_refresh? boolean Determines if the campaign needs its blocks refreshed by opening the web-based campaign editor. Deprecated and will always return false.
---@field resendable? boolean Determines if the campaign qualifies to be resent to non-openers.
---@field recipients? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseRecipients List settings for the campaign.
---@field settings? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseSettings The settings for your campaign, including subject, from name, reply-to address, and more.
---@field variate_settings? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettings The settings specific to A/B test campaigns.
---@field tracking? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseTracking The tracking options for a campaign.
---@field rss_opts? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseRssOpts [RSS](https://mailchimp.com/help/share-your-blog-posts-with-mailchimp/) options for a campaign.
---@field ab_split_opts? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOpts [A/B Testing](https://mailchimp.com/help/about-ab-testing-campaigns/) options for a campaign.
---@field social_card? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseSocialCard The preview for the campaign, rendered by social networks like Facebook and Twitter. [Learn more](https://mailchimp.com/help/enable-and-customize-social-cards/).
---@field report_summary? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseReportSummary For sent campaigns, a summary of opens, clicks, and e-commerce data.
---@field delivery_status? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseDeliveryStatus Updates on campaigns in the process of sending.
---@field resend_shortcut_eligibility? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseResendShortcutEligibility Determines if the campaign qualifies for the Campaign Resend Shortcuts. Only included when query parameter `include_resend_shortcuts` is `true`.
---@field resend_shortcut_usage? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseResendShortcutUsage Information about campaigns related through shortcuts.
---@field _links? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseLinksList A list of link types and descriptions for the API schema documents.

---[A/B Testing](https://mailchimp.com/help/about-ab-testing-campaigns/) options for a campaign.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOpts
---@field split_test? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOptsSplitTest The type of AB split to run.
---@field pick_winner? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOptsPickWinner How we should evaluate a winner. Based on 'opens', 'clicks', or 'manual'.
---@field wait_units? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOptsWaitUnits How unit of time for measuring the winner ('hours' or 'days'). This cannot be changed after a campaign is sent.
---@field wait_time? number The amount of time to wait before picking a winner. This cannot be changed after a campaign is sent.
---@field split_size? number The size of the split groups. Campaigns split based on 'schedule' are forced to have a 50/50 split. Valid split integers are between 1-50.
---@field from_name_a? string For campaigns split on 'From Name', the name for Group A.
---@field from_name_b? string For campaigns split on 'From Name', the name for Group B.
---@field reply_email_a? string For campaigns split on 'From Name', the reply-to address for Group A.
---@field reply_email_b? string For campaigns split on 'From Name', the reply-to address for Group B.
---@field subject_a? string For campaigns split on 'Subject Line', the subject line for Group A.
---@field subject_b? string For campaigns split on 'Subject Line', the subject line for Group B.
---@field send_time_a? string The send time for Group A.
---@field send_time_b? string The send time for Group B.
---@field send_time_winner? string The send time for the winning version.

---How we should evaluate a winner. Based on 'opens', 'clicks', or 'manual'.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOptsPickWinner "opens"|"clicks"|"manual"

---The type of AB split to run.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOptsSplitTest "subject"|"from_name"|"schedule"

---How unit of time for measuring the winner ('hours' or 'days'). This cannot be changed after a campaign is sent.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseAbSplitOptsWaitUnits "hours"|"days"

