---The settings specific to A/B test campaigns.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettings
---@field winning_combination_id? string ID for the winning combination.
---@field winning_campaign_id? string ID of the campaign that was sent to the remaining recipients based on the winning combination.
---@field winner_criteria? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsWinnerCriteria The combination that performs the best. This may be determined automatically by click rate, open rate, or total revenue -- or you may choose manually based on the reporting data you find the most valuable. For Multivariate Campaigns testing send_time, winner_criteria is ignored. For Multivariate Campaigns with 'manual' as the winner_criteria, the winner must be chosen in the Mailchimp web application.
---@field wait_time? number The number of minutes to wait before choosing the winning campaign. The value of wait_time must be greater than 0 and in whole hours, specified in minutes.
---@field test_size? number The percentage of recipients to send the test combinations to, must be a value between 10 and 100.
---@field subject_lines? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsSubjectLinesList The possible subject lines to test. If no subject lines are provided, settings.subject_line will be used.
---@field send_times? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsSendTimesList The possible send times to test. The times provided should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. If send_times are provided to test, the test_size will be set to 100% and winner_criteria will be ignored.
---@field from_names? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsFromNamesList The possible from names. The number of from_names provided must match the number of reply_to_addresses. If no from_names are provided, settings.from_name will be used.
---@field reply_to_addresses? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsReplyToAddressesList The possible reply-to addresses. The number of reply_to_addresses provided must match the number of from_names. If no reply_to_addresses are provided, settings.reply_to will be used.
---@field contents? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsContentsList Descriptions of possible email contents. To set campaign contents, make a PUT request to /campaigns/{campaign_id}/content with the field 'variate_contents'.
---@field combinations? mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsCombinationsList Combinations of possible variables used to build emails.

---@class mailchimp.marketing.CreateCampaignResponseVariateSettingsCombinationsItem
---@field id? string Unique ID for the combination.
---@field subject_line? number The index of `variate_settings.subject_lines` used.
---@field send_time? number The index of `variate_settings.send_times` used.
---@field from_name? number The index of `variate_settings.from_names` used.
---@field reply_to? number The index of `variate_settings.reply_to_addresses` used.
---@field content_description? number The index of `variate_settings.contents` used.
