---@field member_count? number The number of active members in the list.
---@field total_contacts? number An approximate count of subscribed, unsubscribed, and transactional contacts in the list. Does not include cleaned, archived, pending, or contacts that need to be reconfirmed. Requires the (deprecated) include_total_contacts query parameter to be included; for a complete audience contact count, use the /audiences endpoint instead.
---@field unsubscribe_count? number The number of members who have unsubscribed from the list.
---@field cleaned_count? number The number of members cleaned from the list.
---@field member_count_since_send? number The number of active members in the list since the last campaign was sent.
---@field unsubscribe_count_since_send? number The number of members who have unsubscribed since the last campaign was sent.
---@field cleaned_count_since_send? number The number of members cleaned from the list since the last campaign was sent.
---@field campaign_count? number The number of campaigns in any status that use this list.
---@field campaign_last_sent? string The date and time the last campaign was sent to this list in ISO 8601 format. This is updated when a campaign is sent to 10 or more recipients.
---@field merge_field_count? number The number of merge fields ([audience field](https://mailchimp.com/help/getting-started-with-merge-tags/)) for this list (doesn't include EMAIL).
---@field avg_sub_rate? number The average number of subscriptions per month for the list (not returned if we haven't calculated it yet).
---@field avg_unsub_rate? number The average number of unsubscriptions per month for the list (not returned if we haven't calculated it yet).
---@field target_sub_rate? number The target number of subscriptions per month for the list to keep it growing (not returned if we haven't calculated it yet).
---@field open_rate? number The average open rate (a percentage represented as a number between 0 and 100) per campaign for the list (not returned if we haven't calculated it yet).
---@field click_rate? number The average click rate (a percentage represented as a number between 0 and 100) per campaign for the list (not returned if we haven't calculated it yet).
---@field last_sub_date? string The date and time of the last time someone subscribed to this list in ISO 8601 format.
---@field last_unsub_date? string The date and time of the last time someone unsubscribed from this list in ISO 8601 format.

