---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignResponseVariateSettingsWinnerCriteria "opens"|"clicks"|"manual"|"total_revenue"

---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequest
---@field fields? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestFieldsList A comma-separated list of fields to return. Reference parameters of sub-objects with dot notation.
---@field exclude_fields? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestExcludeFieldsList A comma-separated list of fields to exclude. Reference parameters of sub-objects with dot notation.
---@field count? number The number of records to return. Default value is 10. Maximum value is 1000
---@field offset? number Used for [pagination](https://mailchimp.com/developer/marketing/docs/methods-parameters/#pagination), this is the number of records from a collection to skip. Default value is 0.
---@field type? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestType|string The campaign type.
---@field status? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestStatus|string The status of the campaign.
---@field before_send_time? string Restrict the response to campaigns sent before the set time. Uses ISO 8601 time format: 2015-10-21T15:41:36+00:00.
---@field since_send_time? string Restrict the response to campaigns sent after the set time. Uses ISO 8601 time format: 2015-10-21T15:41:36+00:00.
---@field before_create_time? string Restrict the response to campaigns created before the set time. Uses ISO 8601 time format: 2015-10-21T15:41:36+00:00.
---@field since_create_time? string Restrict the response to campaigns created after the set time. Uses ISO 8601 time format: 2015-10-21T15:41:36+00:00.
---@field list_id? string The unique id for the list.
---@field folder_id? string The unique folder id.
---@field member_id? string Retrieve campaigns sent to a particular list member. Member ID is The MD5 hash of the lowercase version of the list member’s email address.
---@field sort_field? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestSortField|string Returns files sorted by the specified field.
---@field sort_dir? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestSortDir|string Determines the order direction for sorted results.
---@field include_resend_shortcut_eligibility? boolean Return the `resend_shortcut_eligibility` field in the response, which tells you if the campaign is eligible for the various Campaign Resend Shortcuts offered.
---@field include_resend_shortcut_usage? boolean Return the `resend_shortcut_usage` field in the response. This includes information about campaigns related by a shortcut.

---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestExcludeFieldsList string[]

---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestFieldsList string[]

---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestSortDir "ASC"|"DESC"

---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestSortField "create_time"|"send_time"

---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestStatus "save"|"paused"|"schedule"|"sending"|"sent"

---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsRequestType "regular"|"plaintext"|"absplit"|"rss"|"variate"

