---@field frequency? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsFrequency The frequency of the RSS Campaign.
---@field schedule? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsSchedule The schedule for sending the RSS Campaign.
---@field last_sent? string The date the campaign was last sent.
---@field constrain_rss_img? boolean Whether to add CSS to images in the RSS feed to constrain their width in campaigns.

---The frequency of the RSS Campaign.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsFrequency "daily"|"weekly"|"monthly"

---The schedule for sending the RSS Campaign.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsSchedule
---@field hour? number The hour to send the campaign in local time. Acceptable hours are 0-23. For example, '4' would be 4am in [your account's default time zone](https://mailchimp.com/help/set-account-defaults/).
---@field daily_send? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsScheduleDailySend The days of the week to send a daily RSS Campaign.
---@field weekly_send_day? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsScheduleWeeklySendDay The day of the week to send a weekly RSS Campaign.
---@field monthly_send_date? number The day of the month to send a monthly RSS Campaign. Acceptable days are 0-31, where '0' is always the last day of a month. Months with fewer than the selected number of days will not have an RSS campaign sent out that day. For example, RSS Campaigns set to send on the 30th will not go out in February.

---The days of the week to send a daily RSS Campaign.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsScheduleDailySend
---@field sunday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Sundays.
---@field monday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Mondays.
---@field tuesday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Tuesdays.
---@field wednesday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Wednesdays.
---@field thursday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Thursdays.
---@field friday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Fridays.
---@field saturday? boolean Sends the daily RSS Campaign on Saturdays.

---The day of the week to send a weekly RSS Campaign.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemRssOptsScheduleWeeklySendDay "sunday"|"monday"|"tuesday"|"wednesday"|"thursday"|"friday"|"saturday"

---The settings for your campaign, including subject, from name, reply-to address, and more.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemSettings
---@field subject_line? string The subject line for the campaign.
---@field preview_text? string The preview text for the campaign.
---@field title? string The title of the campaign.
---@field from_name? string The 'from' name on the campaign (not an email address).
---@field reply_to? string The reply-to email address for the campaign.
---@field use_conversation? boolean Use Mailchimp Conversation feature to manage out-of-office replies.
---@field to_name? string The campaign's custom 'To' name. Typically the first name [audience field](https://mailchimp.com/help/getting-started-with-merge-tags/).
---@field folder_id? string If the campaign is listed in a folder, the id for that folder.
---@field authenticate? boolean Whether Mailchimp [authenticated](https://mailchimp.com/help/about-email-authentication/) the campaign. Defaults to `true`.
---@field auto_footer? boolean Automatically append Mailchimp's [default footer](https://mailchimp.com/help/about-campaign-footers/) to the campaign.
---@field inline_css? boolean Automatically inline the CSS included with the campaign content.
---@field auto_tweet? boolean Automatically tweet a link to the [campaign archive](https://mailchimp.com/help/about-email-campaign-archives-and-pages/) page when the campaign is sent.
---@field auto_fb_post? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemSettingsAutoFbPostList An array of [Facebook](https://mailchimp.com/help/connect-or-disconnect-the-facebook-integration/) page ids to auto-post to.
---@field fb_comments? boolean Allows Facebook comments on the campaign (also force-enables the Campaign Archive toolbar). Defaults to `true`.
---@field timewarp? boolean Send this campaign using [Timewarp](https://mailchimp.com/help/use-timewarp/).
---@field template_id? number The id for the template used in this campaign.
---@field drag_and_drop? boolean Whether the campaign uses the drag-and-drop editor.

---An array of [Facebook](https://mailchimp.com/help/connect-or-disconnect-the-facebook-integration/) page ids to auto-post to.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemSettingsAutoFbPostList string[]

---The preview for the campaign, rendered by social networks like Facebook and Twitter. [Learn more](https://mailchimp.com/help/enable-and-customize-social-cards/).
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemSocialCard
---@field image_url? string The url for the header image for the card.
---@field description? string A short summary of the campaign to display.
---@field title? string The title for the card. Typically the subject line of the campaign.

---The current status of the campaign.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemStatus "save"|"paused"|"schedule"|"sending"|"sent"|"canceled"|"canceling"|"archived"

---The tracking options for a campaign.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemTracking
---@field opens? boolean Whether to [track opens](https://mailchimp.com/help/about-open-tracking/). Defaults to `true`. Cannot be set to false for variate campaigns.
---@field html_clicks? boolean Whether to [track clicks](https://mailchimp.com/help/enable-and-view-click-tracking/) in the HTML version of the campaign. Defaults to `true`. Cannot be set to false for variate campaigns.
---@field text_clicks? boolean Whether to [track clicks](https://mailchimp.com/help/enable-and-view-click-tracking/) in the plain-text version of the campaign. Defaults to `true`. Cannot be set to false for variate campaigns.
---@field goal_tracking? boolean Deprecated
---@field ecomm360? boolean Whether to enable e-commerce tracking.
---@field google_analytics? string The custom slug for [Google Analytics](https://mailchimp.com/help/integrate-google-analytics-with-mailchimp/) tracking (max of 50 bytes).
---@field clicktale? string The custom slug for [ClickTale](https://mailchimp.com/help/additional-tracking-options-for-campaigns/) tracking (max of 50 bytes).
---@field salesforce? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemTrackingSalesforce Deprecated
---@field capsule? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemTrackingCapsule Deprecated

---Deprecated
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemTrackingCapsule
---@field notes? boolean Update contact notes for a campaign based on subscriber email addresses.

---Deprecated
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemTrackingSalesforce
---@field campaign? boolean Create a campaign in a connected Salesforce account.
---@field notes? boolean Update contact notes for a campaign based on subscriber email addresses.

---There are four types of [campaigns](https://mailchimp.com/help/getting-started-with-campaigns/) you can create in Mailchimp. A/B Split campaigns have been deprecated and variate campaigns should be used instead.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemType "regular"|"plaintext"|"absplit"|"rss"|"variate"

---The settings specific to A/B test campaigns.
---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettings
---@field winning_combination_id? string ID for the winning combination.
---@field winning_campaign_id? string ID of the campaign that was sent to the remaining recipients based on the winning combination.
---@field winner_criteria? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsWinnerCriteria The combination that performs the best. This may be determined automatically by click rate, open rate, or total revenue -- or you may choose manually based on the reporting data you find the most valuable. For Multivariate Campaigns testing send_time, winner_criteria is ignored. For Multivariate Campaigns with 'manual' as the winner_criteria, the winner must be chosen in the Mailchimp web application.
---@field wait_time? number The number of minutes to wait before choosing the winning campaign. The value of wait_time must be greater than 0 and in whole hours, specified in minutes.
---@field test_size? number The percentage of recipients to send the test combinations to, must be a value between 10 and 100.
---@field subject_lines? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsSubjectLinesList The possible subject lines to test. If no subject lines are provided, settings.subject_line will be used.
---@field send_times? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsSendTimesList The possible send times to test. The times provided should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. If send_times are provided to test, the test_size will be set to 100% and winner_criteria will be ignored.
---@field from_names? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsFromNamesList The possible from names. The number of from_names provided must match the number of reply_to_addresses. If no from_names are provided, settings.from_name will be used.
---@field reply_to_addresses? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsReplyToAddressesList The possible reply-to addresses. The number of reply_to_addresses provided must match the number of from_names. If no reply_to_addresses are provided, settings.reply_to will be used.
---@field contents? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsContentsList Descriptions of possible email contents. To set campaign contents, make a PUT request to /campaigns/{campaign_id}/content with the field 'variate_contents'.
---@field combinations? mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsCombinationsList Combinations of possible variables used to build emails.

---@class mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsCombinationsItem
---@field id? string Unique ID for the combination.
---@field subject_line? number The index of `variate_settings.subject_lines` used.
---@field send_time? number The index of `variate_settings.send_times` used.
---@field from_name? number The index of `variate_settings.from_names` used.
---@field reply_to? number The index of `variate_settings.reply_to_addresses` used.
---@field content_description? number The index of `variate_settings.contents` used.
---@field recipients? number The number of recipients for this combination.

---Combinations of possible variables used to build emails.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsCombinationsList mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsCombinationsItem[]

---Descriptions of possible email contents. To set campaign contents, make a PUT request to /campaigns/{campaign_id}/content with the field 'variate_contents'.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsContentsList string[]

---The possible from names. The number of from_names provided must match the number of reply_to_addresses. If no from_names are provided, settings.from_name will be used.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsFromNamesList string[]

---The possible reply-to addresses. The number of reply_to_addresses provided must match the number of from_names. If no reply_to_addresses are provided, settings.reply_to will be used.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsReplyToAddressesList string[]

---The possible send times to test. The times provided should be in the format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS. If send_times are provided to test, the test_size will be set to 100% and winner_criteria will be ignored.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsSendTimesList string[]

---The possible subject lines to test. If no subject lines are provided, settings.subject_line will be used.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsSubjectLinesList string[]

---The combination that performs the best. This may be determined automatically by click rate, open rate, or total revenue -- or you may choose manually based on the reporting data you find the most valuable. For Multivariate Campaigns testing send_time, winner_criteria is ignored. For Multivariate Campaigns with 'manual' as the winner_criteria, the winner must be chosen in the Mailchimp web application.
---@alias mailchimp.marketing.GetCampaignsResponseCampaignsItemVariateSettingsWinnerCriteria "opens"|"clicks"|"manual"|"total_revenue"

